From 8bccf79953fb21ae79910e46de54bad787c2b265 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: johannSo <jzeug@soppa.de>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 10:07:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: Add the OnePlus 7T Pro's camera sensors

The OnePlus 7T Pro's cameras are a Sony IMX586 (main), a Sony IMX481
(ultrawide), a Samsung S5K3M5 (telephoto) and a Sony IMX471 (front, in
the pop-up), captured through Qualcomm CAMSS and the simple pipeline
handler with the software ISP.

Add their camera sensor helpers: a black level of 64 at 10 bits (the
pedestal the phone's vendor camera files give), Sony's analogue gain
1024 / (1024 - code) for the three Sony sensors, and for the S5K3M5 the
whole-step gain its kernel driver takes (1x to 16x). Add their sensor
properties: the unit cells the sensors' makers give (0.8 um for the
IMX586, 1.0 um for the others) and two-frame control delays. The test
pattern numbering is not listed.

Add uncalibrated tuning files for the simple IPA: the identity colour
matrix so the saturation default applies, contrast 1.2 and saturation
1.1 as on the other phones, luma and chroma noise reduction scaled with
the gain, and contrast autofocus on the main camera (LC898217XC lens),
the ultrawide (AK7374) and the telephoto (LC898217XC). The front camera
has fixed focus.

Nothing changes for the other sensors: the helpers, properties and
tuning files are new entries only.

The IMX481 values (its helper and imx481.yaml, autofocus included) are
the OnePlus 7T Pro's. The Pixel 4 XL's rear telephoto is an IMX481 too,
and its kernel driver names it imx481, so it takes the same helper and
tuning file, with autofocus tuned for the 7T Pro's AK7374 lens.
